Z||000014||wkayl||09-04-2001||09:19 PM||||Hangover cure.  The next morning stand in the shower and turn on the COLD water until you can't breath.  It works every time for me (although I'm getting to the age where I'm smarter and don't do it as often).<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg"> <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||6
Z||000015||DaRkLoRD||09-04-2001||10:36 PM||||lots of water... and something to absorb alcohol, many people use bread, but there are herbal supplements such as psillyum (psyllium?) that expand after you ingest them, their purpose is to help clean out your intestinal tract.. if they become absorbant, they might also be useful for taking some of the alcohol out of your stomach..<P>but I rarely drink, so I've not yet had a chance to try this out.. but water does work.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000016||Shiner||09-05-2001||12:43 AM||||Hair of the dog really works.  Of course if you have to be at work that morning, you can't really go in plastered.  But if there is no work...  I went on a week long bender last spring break.  I would get up, drink 4 more beers, and everything would be great!  Of course, after a week of this, my stomach got pretty PO'd.  I think the hangover lasted 3 days from when I quit drinking.  Uhg.<P>  If it's not more than 12 or so drinks, a couple Cokes and some eggs and bacon fix me right up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000017||JohnnyK||09-05-2001||02:21 AM||||Sleeper: Course, that same friend died from drinking a lot and then going swimming. sigh..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> But anyways, I am coming to the realization that there is no cure, except drinking lots of water and eating some food, and waiting (the last thing being the worst)..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000018||Butter||09-05-2001||01:23 PM||||Well I can say good moonshine give me the most respect for alcohol.<BR>But now one of the best cures I've heard of is my friends Dad's cure.  So my friend wanted to know what it was like to get drunk for the first time.  My friend's Dad, tring to do the right thing, told his son "Look you don't have to buy the alcohol and I'll get you drunk here at home and I won't let you get into trouble."  My friend considered this to be the safe option to take so they proceeded to get $hit faced.  Next morning my friend had one terrible hangover so he asked his Dad if he could just bring him a hangover remedy since he had the cotton mouth really bad.  So the father fixed him up a glass of vodka all iced down and he drinks about half of it in one swallow before he realizes then proceeds to puke his guts out.  After he gets back to his senses he asked his father why he did such a mean trick on him.  His father asked him if he wanted  anything alcoholic to drink.  His answer was NO.  His Dad said that will cure all the rest of your hangovers!||||reg||12
Z||000019||JSocha||09-05-2001||02:37 PM||||Beer before liquor,<BR>You've never been sicker.<BR>Liquor before beer,<BR>You're in the clear.<P>Anyhow, Jeff's recipe to avoid hangovers:<P>1.  Don't drink<BR>2.  If you do drink, drink in moderation<P><B><u>WORTHLESS INFORMATION:</u></B><BR>Did you know that if you drink "actual/true" Russian VODKA you will never get a hangover from it because of the purity of the alcohol itself?  Same with good Everclear...as it is extremly pure.<P>True Russian alcohol has neither taste, smell nor color.  Unlike Smirnoff, Phillips, Absolute (- <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">-)or other brands of domestic VODKA to which there is a slight, bitter, sharp taste.  That's the chemicals they use in the fermentation process that you taste and/or smell.<P>Most domestic alcohols and beers contain perservatives and other chemicals which are the leading cause of hangovers experienced after drinking.  <P>Imported beers, that are naturally fermented, without the use of chemicals and/or perservatives, you are far less likely to get the "morning after" feeling of a hangover.<P>My father went back to Germany in '87, brought back German beer and 6 bottles of real Russian Vodka.  Excellant Vodka!  I have a hard time drinking the other domestic Vodka now!<P>True Mexican Tequila does not contain a worm in any bottle.  That was a custom added later by other Tequila producers.<P>A true, long-term vetran alcoholic can drink rubbing alcohol straight (yuck in my book when I heard that).<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
